<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Résumé" description="Résumé of Mateus Reis Bastos, an IT Infrastructure Intern and Communication Network Engineering student at UnB.">
  <div class="resume-page shell">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>Mateus Reis Bastos</h1>
      <p>IT Infrastructure Intern · Blue Team, SOC and cybersecurity · Network Engineering — UnB</p>
      <div class="resume-contact" aria-label="Location and career objective">
        <span>Brasília, Federal District, Brazil</span>
        <span>Seeking an information-security internship — on-site, hybrid, or remote</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="resume-section">
      <h2>Profile</h2>
      <div>
        <p class="resume-intro">Communication Network Engineering student at the University of Brasília, focused on information security and infrastructure. I am building hands-on experience in monitoring, access control, and observability, combining a defensive SOC perspective with CTF practice and offensive-security studies.</p>
        <p>I currently work at Associação GigaCandanga and am part of the management team at UnBreakable, UnB's offensive-security study group. I am seeking an information-security internship in Brasília or remotely.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-section">
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <div>
        <article class="resume-entry">
          <header>
            <h3>SOC Intern</h3>
            <p>Associação GigaCandanga · Nov 2025 – Mar 2026 · Brasília, Brazil · hybrid</p>
          </header>
          <p>GigaCandanga is a Science and Technology Institution (ICT) responsible for managing Redecomep, the metropolitan education and research network of Brazil's Federal District. It provides high-speed fiber-optic infrastructure connecting UnB, research institutes, and government agencies in the Federal District.</p>
          <p>I joined the <strong>SOC-as-a-Service</strong> project, based on a multi-tenant architecture, under the guidance of my first supervisor.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Participated in the project's initial structuring stage through study and review of its technical proposal and documentation.</li>
            <li>Researched public threat-indicator (IOC) feeds as input for future integration with detection tools.</li>
            <li>Developed a complete project glossary of approximately 90 terms, covering threats and attack indicators; SOC, monitoring, and defense concepts; networks and protocols; packet and traffic analysis; security tools (SIEM/IDS/IPS/SOAR); multi-tenant architecture; and open-source licensing models — used as reference material for service clients.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> Wazuh · Threat Intelligence (IOCs)</p>
          <aside class="accuracy-note" aria-label="Accuracy note"><strong>Accuracy note.</strong> During this period, only Wazuh was used in practice. The technical glossary covers a much broader set of tools — this reflects research and documentation, not hands-on experience with every tool.</aside>
        </article>

        <article class="resume-entry">
          <header>
            <h3>IT Infrastructure Intern</h3>
            <p>Associação GigaCandanga · Mar 2026 – present · Brasília, Brazil · hybrid</p>
          </header>
          <p>After my original supervisor left, I began working more broadly in IT infrastructure.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>SOC architecture and planning:</strong> mapping security tools (SIEM/XDR) to compose the cyber-defense structure.</li>
            <li>Laboratory proofs of concept (PoCs) for security monitoring and log analysis using Wazuh, Suricata, and Docker Compose — deployment tests on infrastructure with three dedicated servers (Wazuh, Zabbix, and JumpServer), validating endpoint integration and Security Configuration Assessment (SCA) processes.</li>
            <li>Studied and validated JumpServer as a Privileged Access Management (PAM) solution: Bastion Host configuration, session auditing, and secure SSH policies.</li>
            <li>Linux system administration and operation of Zabbix and Grafana for high-capacity network monitoring.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> Wazuh · Suricata · Docker · Linux · JumpServer · Zabbix · Grafana · TCP/IP · DNS · Firewall · Python</p>
          <aside class="accuracy-note" aria-label="Accuracy note"><strong>Accuracy note.</strong> Laboratory / proof-of-concept environment; it does not represent a production deployment.</aside>
        </article>

        <article class="resume-entry">
          <header>
            <h3>Management team member and Recon instructor — UnBreakable</h3>
            <p>UnB offensive-security study group · Mar 2026 – present</p>
          </header>
          <p>UnBreakable is the University of Brasília's offensive-security study group, created to develop cybersecurity in academia and train competitors for national and international challenges. It holds hands-on sessions on Hack The Box and TryHackMe machines, produces write-ups, participates in CTFs, and organizes technical talks with researchers and security professionals.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Part of the management team responsible for structuring and running the 2026 selection process (eliminatory hands-on challenges, a mandatory write-up as the final criterion, and 29 approved candidates) and organizing the group's activities.</li>
            <li>One of the instructors for the entry-level cohort (Recon), leading weekly hands-on sessions on TryHackMe machines, each accompanied by a technical write-up.</li>
            <li>Help organize technical talks with researchers and security professionals.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="resume-entry">
          <header>
            <h3>Member — IEEE ComSoc UnB</h3>
            <p>IEEE Communications Society student chapter · May 2025 – Mar 2026</p>
          </header>
          <p>IEEE ComSoc UnB is the Communications Society student chapter at the University of Brasília, focused on projects and events related to communication networks.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Participated in communication-networking projects and events.</li>
            <li>Worked on the volunteer team for the IEEE ComSoc Student Leadership Tech Conference Centro-Norte Brasil (Oct. 2025), supporting the event's organization and delivery — talks and workshops on networks, cybersecurity, blockchain, and spectrum regulation.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="resume-entry">
          <header>
            <h3>Trainee — IEEE ComSoc UnB</h3>
            <p>IEEE Communications Society student chapter · Mar 2025 – May 2025</p>
          </header>
          <p>Final stage of the selection process to become an effective member of the IEEE ComSoc UnB student chapter.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Co-developed, with other trainees, a project proposal to democratize internet access through Mesh networks using low-cost equipment.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
